{"id":"CVE-2021-3115","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2021-01-26T02:14:51.000Z","updated":"2024-08-03T16:45:51.223Z","description":"Go before 1.14.14 and 1.15.x before 1.15.7 on Windows is vulnerable to Command Injection and remote code execution when using the \"go get\" command to fetch modules that make use of cgo (for example, cgo can execute a gcc program from an untrusted download).","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/mperVMGa98w","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://blog.golang.org/path-security","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/YWAYJGXWC232SG3UR3TR574E6BP3OSQQ/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-e435a8bb88"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20210219-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202208-02","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202208-02"}],"vendors":["golang","microsoft"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4235","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2022-12-27T21:13:42.393Z","updated":"2025-04-11T16:25:11.371Z","title":"Denial of service in gopkg.in/yaml.v2","description":"Due to unbounded alias chasing, a maliciously crafted YAML file can cause the system to consume significant system resources. If parsing user input, this may be used as a denial of service vector.","cwe":["CWE 400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":5.5,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"gopkg.in/yaml.v2","product":"gopkg.in/yaml.v2","packageName":"gopkg.in/yaml.v2","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <2.2.3 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"github.com/go-yaml/yaml","product":"github.com/go-yaml/yaml","packageName":"github.com/go-yaml/yaml","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"affected"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/go-yaml/yaml/pull/375"},{"url":"https://github.com/go-yaml/yaml/commit/bb4e33bf68bf89cad44d386192cbed201f35b241"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2021-0061"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/07/msg00001.html"}],"credits":["@simonferquel"],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4236","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2022-12-27T21:13:45.711Z","updated":"2025-04-11T16:20:55.821Z","title":"Panic or authentication bypass in github.com/ecnepsnai/web","description":"Web Sockets do not execute any AuthenticateMethod methods which may be set, leading to a nil pointer dereference if the returned UserData pointer is assumed to be non-nil, or authentication bypass. This issue only affects WebSockets with an AuthenticateMethod hook. Request handlers that do not explicitly use WebSockets are not vulnerable.","cwe":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"github.com/ecnepsnai/web","product":"github.com/ecnepsnai/web","packageName":"github.com/ecnepsnai/web","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 1.4.0 <1.5.2 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/ecnepsnai/web/commit/5a78f8d5c41ce60dcf9f61aaf47a7a8dc3e0002f"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2021-0107"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4238","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2022-12-27T21:13:50.373Z","updated":"2025-04-11T16:17:46.299Z","title":"Insufficient randomness in github.com/Masterminds/goutils","description":"Randomly-generated alphanumeric strings contain significantly less entropy than expected. The RandomAlphaNumeric and CryptoRandomAlphaNumeric functions always return strings containing at least one digit from 0 to 9. This significantly reduces the amount of entropy in short strings generated by these functions.","cwe":["CWE 330: Use of Insufficiently Random Values"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":9.1,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"github.com/Masterminds/goutils","product":"github.com/Masterminds/goutils","packageName":"github.com/Masterminds/goutils","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.1.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/Masterminds/goutils/commit/869801f20f9f1e7ecdbdb6422049d8241270d5e1"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2022-0411"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4239","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2022-12-27T21:13:53.590Z","updated":"2025-04-14T16:59:43.688Z","title":"Weak encryption and denial of service in github.com/flynn/noise","description":"The Noise protocol implementation suffers from weakened cryptographic security after encrypting 2^64 messages, and a potential denial of service attack. After 2^64 (~18.4 quintillion) messages are encrypted with the Encrypt function, the nonce counter will wrap around, causing multiple messages to be encrypted with the same key and nonce. In a separate issue, the Decrypt function increments the nonce state even when it fails to decrypt a message. If an attacker can provide an invalid input to the Decrypt function, this will cause the nonce state to desynchronize between the peers, resulting in a failure to encrypt all subsequent messages.","cwe":["CWE 400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"github.com/flynn/noise","product":"github.com/flynn/noise","packageName":"github.com/flynn/noise","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.0.0 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/flynn/noise/pull/44"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2022-0425"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4272","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"VulDB","published":"2022-12-21T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-14T17:29:02.619Z","title":"studygolang topics.js cross site scripting","description":"A vulnerability classified as problematic has been found in studygolang. This affects an unknown part of the file static/js/topics.js. The manipulation of the argument contentHtml leads to cross site scripting. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. The name of the patch is 0fb30f9640bd5fa0cae58922eac6c00bb1a94391. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The identifier VDB-216477 was assigned to this vulnerability.","cwe":["CWE-707 CWE-707 Improper Neutralization -> CWE-74 Injection -> CWE-79 Cross Site Scripting"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":3.5,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"unspecified","product":"studygolang","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/studygolang/studygolang/commit/0fb30f9640bd5fa0cae58922eac6c00bb1a94391"},{"url":"https://vuldb.com/?id.216477"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2021-4273","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"VulDB","published":"2022-12-21T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-14T17:28:48.709Z","title":"studygolang search.go Search cross site scripting","description":"A vulnerability classified as problematic was found in studygolang. This vulnerability affects the function Search of the file http/controller/search.go. The manipulation of the argument q leads to cross site scripting. The attack can be initiated remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The name of the patch is 97ba556d42fa89dfaa7737e9cd3a8ddaf670bb23. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. VDB-216478 is the identifier assigned to this vulnerability.","cwe":["CWE-707 CWE-707 Improper Neutralization -> CWE-74 Injection -> CWE-79 Cross Site Scripting"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":4.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"unspecified","product":"studygolang","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/studygolang/studygolang/pull/158"},{"url":"https://github.com/studygolang/studygolang/commit/97ba556d42fa89dfaa7737e9cd3a8ddaf670bb23"},{"url":"https://vuldb.com/?id.216478"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
