{"id":"CVE-2021-41087","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2021-09-21T21:05:15.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T02:59:31.359Z","title":"Improperly Implemented path matching for in-toto-golang","description":"in-toto-golang is a go implementation of the in-toto framework to protect software supply chain integrity. In affected versions authenticated attackers posing as functionaries (i.e., within a trusted set of users for a layout) are able to create attestations that may bypass DISALLOW rules in the same layout. An attacker with access to trusted private keys, may issue an attestation that contains a disallowed artifact by including path traversal semantics (e.g., foo vs dir/../foo). Exploiting this vulnerability is dependent on the specific policy applied. The problem has been fixed in version 0.3.0.","cwe":["CWE-345 CWE-345: Insufficient Verification of Data Authenticity"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.6,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"in-toto","product":"in-toto-golang","versions":["affected < 0.3.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/in-toto/in-toto-golang/security/advisories/GHSA-vrxp-mg9f-hwf3","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/in-toto/in-toto-golang/commit/f2c57d1e0f15e3ffbeac531829c696b72ecc4290","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["golang"]}
